Difference between Open source models and closed source models

opensource model - open source llms make their model weights, architecture, and sometimes training code publicly avaliable.Anyone
can download,run,modify,fine-tune or redistribute them. 
Can be run locally on your hardware.
No per-token API costs(after hardware investment) 
examples : (LLaMA 3.1, Mistral7B, Gemma2, Falcon, Phi-3, DeepSeek R1)

Closedsource model - closed source llms keep theor weights, architecture, and training data proprietary. You access them only 
through an API. Paying per token/request. You cannot download or modify the model.
No infrastructure managemnet
Always up-to-date (provider handles updates)
Typically highest performance out-of-the box.
Enterprice suppport and SLA's available.
examples : (GPT, Claude, Gemini)


